$.tables.content.2.sections.1.body.2.text
  - "Orla now has gearing of 33.3% and an acid test of 0.7:1. Neither is alarming for a bakery with daily cash sales and loans costing less than its ROCE. But a second loan-financed bakery would first add interest owed to the bank every month, even in a year when sales fell; then, at the year end, the statement of financial position would show gearing pushed higher. Issuing new shares would keep gearing down, at the cost of sharing future profit with more owners."
  + "Orla now has gearing of 33.3% and an acid test of 0.7:1. Neither is alarming for a bakery with daily cash sales and loans costing less than its ROCE. But a second loan-financed bakery would first add interest owed to the bank every month; then, at the year end, the statement of financial position would show gearing pushed higher; and if sales fell in the year after that, the interest would still be owed. Issuing new shares would keep gearing down, at the cost of sharing future profit with more owners."
